# CLAUDE.md — rules for game agents in this repo

This repo is **one game**, `{{name}}`, published as its own Roblox experience and built on
**StudWork**. It is a StudWork *single-game project*: the repository root is the game, and StudWork
lives in the git submodule `studwork/`, pinned at a release tag (`{{tag}}`). Language: **Luau,
`--!strict`**.

Read, inside the submodule: `studwork/docs/philosophy.md` (why it is opinionated),
`studwork/docs/framework/` (start with `getting-started.md`; `single-game-project.md` explains this
repo's setup) and `studwork/docs/framework/module-api.md` (the source of truth for the module API).
This repo's own docs: `README.md`, `docs/design.md`, `FRAMEWORK_REQUESTS.md`.

## Hard rules

1. **Never edit `studwork/`** (framework, kits, ui, vendor, tools, docs: anything in it). Game work
   happens on a feature branch (e.g. `game/<topic>`). `tools/lint` fails if the submodule is not at
   exactly a release tag or has local changes, and the `packages` guardrail refuses a `studwork`
   change on a `game/*` branch or the pointer staged together with any other file. Need something?
   Add an entry to `FRAMEWORK_REQUESTS.md` (or open an issue on the StudWork repository); the
   framework ships it in a release, then the pointer is bumped in its own commit (README.md, "Bump
   StudWork"). If you changed something there by accident: `git -C studwork checkout -- .`.
2. **The module API is not yours to change.** Use what the pinned tag documents; additive changes are
   requested in `FRAMEWORK_REQUESTS.md`.
3. **The server is authoritative.** Clients only send requests (module actions, §9). The server
   validates every argument (type, range, ownership) and every action is rate-limited by the
   framework's Net. Never trust amounts, item ids, uids, prices or positions from a client. Robux
   purchases go through `ctx.shop.onProduct` (receipt-safe, data-only handlers, see "Purchases"),
   never through a remote.
4. **Every balance number lives in the game's Config** (`src/shared/Config`): kit settings in
   `config.<Module>` (`Balance.luau`), game-own numbers in `Tuning.luau`. Modules read their config
   from `ctx.config`; kits ship opinionated defaults, documented on each kit page.
5. **No secrets in the repo.** Open Cloud keys come from env vars or the git-ignored `.env`. No
   absolute paths in committed files either.
6. **Libraries come from StudWork.** This repo has no `wally.toml` / `rokit.toml`: Wally packages and
   tool versions are StudWork's pins (`studwork/deps/wally.toml`, `studwork/rokit.toml`). Need a new
   library? File a `FRAMEWORK_REQUESTS.md` entry; don't add pins here.
7. **Git:** feature branches, local commits only unless the user asks otherwise. Never push or add
   remotes without being asked. Commit only your own paths; never `--no-verify`.
8. **Paid random items** (Compliance, module-api §14 and §19.6–19.7):
   - Odds are always disclosed: every random source registers with `ctx.compliance`; players see the
     server's odds (mutations, pity, luck) in the odds UI. Never recompute odds on the client.
   - Paid rolls go only through `ctx.compliance.roll` (inside a purchase) or
     `ctx.compliance.spendForRoll` (priced in a currency listed in `compliance.paidCurrencies`). A
     paid currency spent on a non-random good goes through `ctx.compliance.spendPaid`; any roll later
     in that tx counts as paid. `Economy.spend` refuses paid currencies.
   - A paid roll needs the source's odds already sent to that player's client (a purchase without
     them is retried). Luck other than 1 on a paid roll is refused unless the table has
     `luckDisclosed = true` and the client received odds computed with that exact luck. Give luck
     with `Rarity.setLuck`, never as a hidden roll argument. Free rolls may use any luck.
   - Players restricted by `PolicyService` can't buy paid random items: a Robux product handler
     grants a fixed non-random fallback (`tx.paidRandomRestricted`), never takes money for nothing.
     Copies from paid sources are tagged by the framework (`paid:<product>`, `paidcur:<table>`); tags
     can't be forged and those copies can't be traded or mailed.
9. **No text-chat dependence** (chat is age-gated): pings, emotes, roles.
10. **Ask the user** before installing anything outside the repo or with sudo, spending money,
    publishing to Roblox, or touching files outside the repo root.
11. **Nothing is special.** Game modules use only the `StudWork` facade, their `ctx`, the UI kit and
    other modules' public APIs (`StudWork.use(ref)` / `ctx.deps[ref]`). Never require framework
    internals (`ServerScriptService.Framework`), never read or write another module's save section,
    never walk the framework's instances. The `special` guardrail enforces it.
12. **Network only through the framework.** Declare a module's actions/events (§9); never use
    `OnServerEvent`/`OnServerInvoke`, `RemoteEvent`/`RemoteFunction` instances, `ProcessReceipt`,
    `Prompt*PurchaseFinished`, `DataStoreService` or ProfileStore directly. The framework owns
    `ProcessReceipt` exclusively (§7.1).
13. **Full inventory is not a failure.** A Mail handler that can't accept a message now returns
    `false`: the message waits in the player's mailbox with no time limit. Only thrown errors are
    retried and dead-lettered. Handlers must be safe to run twice.
14. **Items are declared in `GameConfig.items`**, validated once at boot. Registering items after
    `StudWork.start` errors (so nothing enters a paid table before its odds are disclosed).
15. **`tools/lint` guardrails must stay clean** (`studwork/docs/framework/guardrails.md`): `modules`,
    `numbers`, `remotes`, `purchases`, `packages` (incl. the framework pin), `special`, `theme`. They
    scan every file Rojo syncs. `-- guard: allow <check>` on a line is a last resort and needs a
    reason on the line above.

